      "part_type": "Hadith",
      "path": "/books/al-kafi:6:2:82:4",
      "text": [
        " أُمِّ وَلَدٍ لِنَصْرَانِيٍّ أَسْلَمَتْ أَ يَتَزَوَّجُهَا الْمُسْلِمُ قَالَ نَعَمْ وَ عِدَّتُهَا مِنَ النَّصْرَانِيِّ إِذَا أَسْلَمَتْ عِدَّةُ الْحُرَّةِ الْمُطَلَّقَةِ ثَلَاثَةُ أَشْهُرٍ أَوْ ثَلَاثَةُ قُرُوءٍ فَإِذَا انْقَضَتْ عِدَّتُهَا فَلْيَتَزَوَّجْهَا إِنْ شَاءَتْ ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "And by his chain, from Ibn Mahboub, from Ali Bin Raib, from Humran, ",
          "(It has been narrated) from Abu Ja’far<sup>asws</sup> regarding a mother of a child of a Christian man, became a Muslim, can the Muslim man marry her?’ He<sup>asws</sup> said: ‘Yes, and her waiting period from the Christian man when she became a Muslim, is a waiting period of the free divorced woman, being of three months, or three <span class=\"iTxt\">Quroos</span> (pure periods). So when she fulfils her waiting period, so let him marry her, if he so desires to’."
        ]
      }
